 third set is *closed* since it contains all its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186409711 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dbcbe48-2124-5037-bac0-c99498ef9fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409698} {:answer/id #uuid "3a63ced9-ca36-5f7e-b7b0-e658c1fa60dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409699} {:answer/id #uuid "408a94f7-529c-5ff0-8b23-26d97a71b99c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409701} {:answer/id #uuid "6e671489-f5be-562e-8530-e27db89c1e00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409704} {:answer/id #uuid "bcc31443-e5f9-544a-84d7-9325a05e998e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409707}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0dbcbe48-2124-5037-bac0-c99498ef9fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409698} :answer-field/id #uuid "6c28df82-226c-551a-9267-de3801bebac5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186409709}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b04f2bd5-de84-5515-a0a5-3d6c81e3d583" :question/math-academy-id "q-161644" :question/problem "Which of the following sets are open?\n\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,1\\le y\\le 2-x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }-1<x<1,\\,0<y<1+x}$\n- ${(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}:\\text{ }4\\le {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\le 9}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that:\n\n- A set is *open* if it does not contain any of its boundary points. In other words, an open set consists only of the interior points of the set.\n\n- A set is *closed* if it contains **all** of its boundary points. In other words, a closed set consists of all the interior and all the boundary points of the set.\n\nLet's examine our sets in turn.\n\n- The first set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\n- The second set is *open* since it doesn't contain any of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are strict).\n\n- The third set is *closed* since it contains all of its boundary points (all the corresponding inequalities are not strict).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278582 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192767 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7adf2c3e-4a73-5098-ab60-790d637728cf" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Open and Closed Sets in the Plane in Set Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f43270e-5fd5-5fe3-b96d-2845968d906e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275762} {:answer/id #uuid "91704fdf-0254-5001-b4f6-f9904429324d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276793} {:answer/id #uuid "ade20714-3320-54e9-8da1-4e2411c22400" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277039} {:answer/id #uuid "edc